WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:15.121
On last day of October, a terrible accident occurred.

2
00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:23.749
Pollyanna was walking home from school when a speeding car hit her.

3
00:00:23.769 --> 00:00:26.752
The driver fled, and no one witnessed the accident.

4
00:00:29.844 --> 00:00:32.987
Luckily, a neighbor soon came upon the unconscious girl.

5
00:00:36.009 --> 00:00:40.873
He carried her home, where a frightened Aunt Polly and sobbing Nancy gently put her to bed.

6
00:00:45.897 --> 00:00:46.397
When Dr.

7
00:00:46.437 --> 00:00:49.920
Warren arrived, Nancy ran to tell Tom, who was raking leaves.

8
00:00:51.241 --> 00:00:52.242
Tom dropped his rake.

9
00:00:52.262 --> 00:00:55.985
"Is she seriously injured?"

10
00:00:56.365 --> 00:00:57.266
His voice shook.

11
00:00:57.286 --> 00:00:59.388
"I don't know!"

12
00:01:01.181 --> 00:01:02.022
Nancy sobbed.

13
00:01:02.042 --> 00:01:08.226
"She has a little cut on her head, but Miss Polly's afraid Pollyanna has internal injuries.

14
00:01:09.226 --> 00:01:12.188
You know, Miss Polly really loves that girl."

15
00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:18.392
Nancy ran back into the house to wait for the doctor's diagnosis.

16
00:01:19.513 --> 00:01:24.256
But all she overheard was that Pollyanna had no broken bones and a nurse would arrive that night.

17
00:01:27.296 --> 00:01:29.637
Later Nancy and Tom were eating supper in the kitchen.

18
00:01:29.657 --> 00:01:36.120
"Dr. Warren sounded very serious and said, 'only time will tell,'" Nancy said.

19
00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:38.240
"What does that mean?"

20
00:01:41.042 --> 00:01:41.862
Tom sighed.

21
00:01:41.882 --> 00:01:45.904
"It means we have to wait."

22
00:01:48.184 --> 00:01:50.125
The next morning Pollyanna woke up.

23
00:01:53.907 --> 00:01:54.627
"Aunt Polly!

24
00:01:55.147 --> 00:01:56.788
Why are you sitting by my bed?

25
00:01:58.132 --> 00:01:59.673
I need to get ready for school."

26
00:02:00.914 --> 00:02:04.476
When Pollyanna tried to sit up, she fell back on her pillow and moaned.

27
00:02:04.496 --> 00:02:10.000
"Why can't I get up?"

28
00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:14.563
"I wouldn't try just yet, dear," Aunt Polly said in a soothing voice.

29
00:02:15.784 --> 00:02:17.105
"What's the matter with me?"

30
00:02:19.467 --> 00:02:23.049
Aunt Polly gave an agonized look at the nurse standing at the window.

31
00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:29.504
The young woman nodded and whispered, "Tell her."

32
00:02:30.025 --> 00:02:31.365
Aunt Polly cleared her throat.

33
00:02:32.946 --> 00:02:35.788
"You were hurt by a car yesterday.

34
00:02:36.968 --> 00:02:38.429
But don't think about that now."

35
00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:46.674
"Hurt? Oh, yes, I walked Pollyanna brushed a hand across her forehead.

36
00:02:46.694 --> 00:02:51.396
"There's a bandage on my head and it hurts!"

37
00:02:55.959 --> 00:02:57.900
dear, just try to rest."

38
00:03:00.228 --> 00:03:05.392
"But, Aunt Polly, my legs feel so so odd.

39
00:03:06.113 --> 00:03:07.594
I can't really feel them."

40
00:03:10.416 --> 00:03:14.259
Aunt Polly struggled to her feet and gave the nurse a look, begging for help.

41
00:03:16.361 --> 00:03:18.182
The nurse approached Pollyanna's bedside.

42
00:03:18.202 --> 00:03:21.365
"Hello," she said cheerfully.

43
00:03:21.385 --> 00:03:25.268
"I'm Miss Hunt, and I'm here to help take care of you."

44
00:03:29.036 --> 00:03:30.217
Pollyanna looked around.

45
00:03:30.237 --> 00:03:34.659
"But I don't want to be taken care of!

46
00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:37.541
I want to go to school tomorrow!"

47
00:03:39.282 --> 00:03:41.063
Aunt Polly gave a stifled cry.

48
00:03:46.746 --> 00:03:51.068
not tomorrow," the nurse said brightly, handing Pollyanna some medicine.

49
00:03:51.088 --> 00:03:53.930
"Let's see if these pills help you."

50
00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:56.231
"All right."

51
00:03:59.628 --> 00:04:01.129
Pollyanna swallowed the medicine.

52
00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:06.992
"But I have to go the day after tomorrow to take exams."

53
00:04:09.234 --> 00:04:11.755
She talked for a few more minutes before falling asleep.

54
00:04:13.556 --> 00:04:16.298
For the next week, Pollyanna slept for most of the time.

55
00:04:18.559 --> 00:04:23.081
When Pollyanna was finally more alert, Aunt Polly explained the accident again.

56
00:04:23.101 --> 00:04:29.846
"So I'm hurt, not sick," Pollyanna said when she finally understood.

57
00:04:29.866 --> 00:04:32.728
"Well, I'm glad of that."

58
00:04:32.748 --> 00:04:35.229
"You're glad?"

59
00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:37.691
asked Aunt Polly, sitting by the bed.

60
00:04:37.711 --> 00:04:43.675
"Yes, I'd much rather have broken legs than be a lifelong invalid like Mrs.

61
00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:48.859
Snow. Broken legs heal, but lifelong invalids don't get better."

62
00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:53.823
Aunt Polly, who had never mentioned broken legs, suddenly stood up.

63
00:04:55.756 --> 00:04:59.799
Walking over to Pollyanna's dressing table, she picked up a hairbrush and put it down.

64
00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:04.382
She did that with one thing after another for no apparent reason.

65
00:05:06.504 --> 00:05:08.946
Pollyanna watched a rainbow dancing on her ceiling.

66
00:05:10.066 --> 00:05:12.168
It came from the prisms hanging in a window.

67
00:05:12.188 --> 00:05:18.532
"I'm glad I don't have smallpox or measles," she said.

68
00:05:18.552 --> 00:05:23.176
"The doctor wouldn't let you in my room because those are contagious.

69
00:05:24.352 --> 00:05:27.615
And I'm glad I don't have appendicitis—that's painful!"

70
00:05:27.635 --> 00:05:33.560
"You seem to be glad about many things."

71
00:05:34.941 --> 00:05:39.144
Aunt Polly's eyes were filled with sorrow as she lovingly gazed at her niece.

72
00:05:39.164 --> 00:05:41.706
"Oh, I am!

73
00:05:42.246 --> 00:05:47.250
Lying here gives me lots of time to think about them and to admire my rainbows.

74
00:05:48.451 --> 00:05:49.913
I'm so glad Mr.

75
00:05:49.973 --> 00:05:51.734
Pendleton gave me those prisms!

76
00:05:52.835 --> 00:05:55.472
But most of all I'm glad I was hurt."

77
00:05:55.492 --> 00:05:58.913
"What a thing to say, dear!"

78
00:05:59.453 --> 00:06:00.594
Aunt Polly exclaimed.

79
00:06:00.614 --> 00:06:03.314
"But it's true."

80
00:06:04.375 --> 00:06:05.975
The little girl laughed softly.

81
00:06:05.995 --> 00:06:10.957
"Since I've been hurt, you've called me 'dear' many times.

82
00:06:12.157 --> 00:06:13.417
You never did that before.

83
00:06:15.018 --> 00:06:18.399
Some of the Ladies' Aiders used to do that, but it's not the same.

84
00:06:19.839 --> 00:06:23.260
Oh, Aunt Polly, I'm so glad you belong to me!"

85
00:06:26.883 --> 00:06:28.807
Just then the nurse appeared with some medicine.

86
00:06:30.751 --> 00:06:34.297
Aunt Polly, her eyes now filled with tears, fled the room.
